---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import damonPlaying from '../assets/about/damon-playing.jpg';
---
<Base title="About — The Session Notes" current="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="about">
      <div class="kicker">About the project</div>
      <h1>Most music writing talks to the famous. This talks to everyone else.</h1>
      <p>The Session Notes is a series of interviews with the people who make music work: the players, teachers, engineers, bookers, managers, and label people doing the daily work of a music career. Each conversation gets into how they got in, how they actually make a living, and what building a life in music really takes.</p>
      <p>New interviews come regularly, and the goal is simple: to build an honest record of the working music world, one conversation at a time.</p>

      <figure class="about-photo">
        <Image src={damonPlaying} alt="Damon Uyehara playing snare drum" widths={[600, 1000, 1400]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" />
      </figure>

      <div class="kicker">About the writer</div>
      <p>The Session Notes is written by Damon Uyehara, a senior at Fremont High School in Sunnyvale, California.</p>
      <p>Damon came up through high school band and drumline. In 2026 he performed as a snare drummer with Blue Devils C in stadiums including the Rose Bowl and Stanford Stadium. That experience sparked a deeper curiosity about how working musicians and artists actually grow, what their creative process looks like, and how the business really works.</p>
      <p>This project is his attempt to find out by talking to the people already inside the industry. Damon plans to build a career in music, supporting artists and contributing to the growth of the scene, and these conversations are where that work begins.</p>

      <a class="back" href="/contact">Get in touch →</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
